{"availability":"available","full":"ecthink/last-train","name":"last-train","description":"Watching the whole MTR network go dark every night,to learn Hong Kong's real last trains. Countdown app+ self-learning open dataset.","category":"Education","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-10T04:45:02Z","updated":"2026-10-17T20:54:12Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://last-train-smoky.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://last-train-smoky.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T00:46:41.114Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T00:46:41.114Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T00:46:41.114Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:44:09.146Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-11T22:38:48.744Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-18T00:46:41.114Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Every night one long job watches the entire MTR network through the Next Train API — polling all 121 line-stations every 3 minutes from 22:30 to 02:10 HKT and recording the final train each station showed before going dark.","The result, data/last-trains.json, is a living public record of Hong Kong's real last trains — learned by observation, not copied from a timetable. It refreshes itself nightly and automatically captures special timetables (festivals, typhoons, extended service).","App: · a full-screen countdown to your last train home."],"features":["collect.mjs — the watcher (no dependencies, Node 20)",".github/workflows/watch.yml — the nightly schedule (several start times; only one has to fire)","data/observations.json — tonight's raw sightings + the times the watcher looked (polls)","data/last-trains.json — the learned dataset (median of up to 14 nights per station/direction)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ecthink/last-train/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"47c5e91d66de9ddfc9df15bf65231b8a943b21917facacd1814b624e945624e4","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:44:09.323Z"},"overviewCheckedA